      <slug></slug>
      <title>Django</title>
      <subtitle></subtitle>
      <track>Python</track>
      <type></type>
      <language></language>
      <abstract>&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;http://www.djangoproject.com/&#34;&gt;Django&lt;/a&gt; is a high-level Python Web framework that encourages rapid development and clean, pragmatic design.&#xA;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA; </abstract>
      <description>&#xA;&lt;p&gt;The talk will cover:&#xA;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt; an overview of the Django web framework&#xA;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt; a small sample application to illustrate how quickly you can solve a real world problem in Django while still having a clean and maintainable code base&#xA;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt; how Dojo can be integrated with Djanjo to give your application some Ajax coolness&#xA;&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt; pointers to get you started with Django in no time&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;&#xA; </description>
      <persons>
          <person id="1871">Pim Van Heuven</person>
      </persons>
      <links></links>
      <video></video>
      <end></end>
  </event>